olcek is a complete island: no crate in the workspace depends on it and the
CLI has no ledger to feed it, so its reporting tail was the second half of
the esik question with the opposite answer. esik had an artifact in the tree
(`training/activation.jsonl`) and every method was a line the ledger file
demanded read; olcek has no artifact - nothing in this repo produces a budget
or a ledger yet - so these accessors described a measurement nobody takes.
Per the settled policy (delete-biased with discretion, zero baseline target,
no speculative exemption), the surface goes; it returns with its first real
caller in the same patch, the way the esik wiring did.

Deleted: `Admitted::is_granted` (the grant-set predicate no caller branches
on; the three `Admitted` variants stay public and matchable), `ordinary_used`
and `closing_used` (per-pool splits of `used`, asserted by nobody but each
other's tests), `headroom` (its test asserted `used` beside it and was deleted
with it, so the surviving `used` covers the arithmetic), `pressure_admissions`
and `was_truncated` (the pressure moment is reported where the caller already
sees it, as the `GrantedUnderPressure` outcome itself; the truncation
question belongs to a report that does not exist yet), and `Ledger::pressure`
- the counter no longer read by any surviving method, kept only for its own
deleted getter, a written-but-never-read field `clippy -D warnings` would
have refused.

Two test-line removals and one test rename are semantic housekeeping, not
cover-up: the pressure-band test was named "counts that it had one" after the
deleted counter; its assertion of `GrantedUnderPressure` plus `refusals`
carries the same claim now, so it is renamed "swallows nothing" rather than
weakened silently. The eviction/closing tests keep asserting what they always
proved through the surviving API (`reserve_left`, `drops`, `verify`).

gates/dead-pub-api.baseline: the six lines deleted in the same patch the
deletions make stale, 40 to 34; README: 334 to 332 recounted from the
applied tree (grep `#[test]`, not decremented by hand).

Not compiled: no cargo in this environment (measured). Floor: all 39 gates
pass on the applied tree (rc=0), including public-api-is-reached at 34/34,
and a line-by-line read of every changed hunk; no doc or crate header
promises a deleted thing (the crate header's "counted as pressure" reads the
outcome, which still exists).
